   "confidence": "medium",
   "notes": "Buff ashlar 1930s-style front at the bend of Downing St, seen almost square-on from the south. Rusticated raised ground floor over a basement (low arched basement lights), arched-head ground-floor windows; regular ~3 m window grid; two bays (x~10-15 and ~33-37) rise into segmental pediments with a large arched window and a stone oriel at first floor. Railing on the parapet. Right end (x>40) is only seen obliquely; symmetry assumed."
